        "calls": 1,
        "text": "The automated system that runs paid tasks on a user's computer now allows the installation of specific software tools, but only when the task's written instructions explicitly list them by name and exact version. This narrow permission replaces the previous blanket ban on adding new tools, ensuring that hidden setup scripts never run and that the user's review of the changes remains complete. The internal testing suite also grew from ten to thirty sample projects, so the system can now check its work against a wider range of common software setups before a task is released to the public.",
